From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:45:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Lay out once for web fonts that finish loading
 together

The document was laid out again for every web font that finished loading.
A family split into unicode-range subsets arrives as many small fonts, one
after the other, and the page was laid out once per frame in which one of
them arrived.

Loads that finish while other web fonts are still loading are now applied
together: once no web font is loading anymore, or 100ms after the first one
finished, which is the block period `font-display: swap` allows. The
`FontFace` promises are settled and `document.fonts.ready` is unblocked when
the loads are applied, so they never resolve before the layout that uses
the fonts.

Testing: Covered by existing tests.

Fork note: last of four patches; meant for upstream, applies unchanged. The
100 ms cap is `WEB_FONT_BATCH_DELAY` in window.rs.

Relies on: the previous patch (`LoadedSuccessfully { affects_laid_out_text }`);
`FontContext::web_fonts_still_loading` counting a load until script
decrements it, so that finished-but-unapplied loads keep
`document.fonts.ready` and screenshot readiness pending; the script thread's
oneshot timers (`GlobalScope::schedule_callback`, `OneshotTimerCallback`).

Drop when upstream stops laying out the whole document once per finished web
font: on the keai page from the Validation line, `-Z relayout-event` on plain
upstream then shows a handful of reflows during font loading instead of one
per arriving font.

Validation: `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 1 css/css-font-loading css/css-fonts html/canvas/element/text html/canvas/offscreen/text` (948 tests) unchanged from the previous patch, and 4 repeats of the timing-sensitive subset (css-font-loading, generic-family-keywords-001/003, variations/at-font-face-font-matching, font-palette-add/-2, matching/, font-size-adjust-006, remove-loaded-font-face-rule, font-face-unicode-range-2) all ran as expected. `-Z relayout-event` on the keai page served at 2 MB/s with 30 ms latency (66 subsets arriving over about a second): 39 -> 16-17 reflows, full invalidations 33 -> 10-11, CPU 1.2 -> 1.04 s (plain ohos-main: 152-163 reflows, 2.3 s). On a PLR-AL00, production build with `--features tracing-hitrace`, `servoperf page <dir> --entry page/xuezhiqian-keai_article.html --ohos --legs servo --only load --iterations 5 --no-instructions --bin <hap>`, whole stack against plain ohos-main: `RanLayout` markers per load 17/40/41/40/38 -> 6/7/8/8/7 (median 40 -> 7); first contentful paint median 1345 -> 1161 ms, inside the 21% spread of 5 loads.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; designed with the maintainer, written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
